{"name":"Seashell Cove","hex":"#104c77","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"seashell","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The empty shell of a marine mollusk.","The animal living inside a seashell."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a very light pink colour, like that of some seashells."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seashell"},{"term":"cove","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hollow in a rock; a cave or cavern. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A concave vault or archway, especially the arch of a ceiling."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To arch over; to build in a hollow concave form; to make in the form of a cove."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cove"}],"entries":[{"title":"Seashell","blocks":[{"text":"A seashell, also known simply as a shell, is a hard, protective outer layer usually created by an animal or organism that lives in the sea. Most seashells are made by mollusks, such as snails, clams, and oysters to protect their soft insides. Empty seashells are often found washed up on beaches by beachcombers. The shells are empty because the animal has died and the soft parts have decomposed or been eaten by another organism."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Conchiglie_Seashells_01.jpg/330px-Conchiglie_Seashells_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seashell","wikidata":"Q213096"},{"title":"Cove","blocks":[{"text":"A cove is a small bay or coastal inlet. They usually have narrow, restricted entrances, are often circular or oval, and are often situated within a larger bay. Small, narrow, sheltered bays, inlets, tidal creeks, or recesses in a coast are often considered coves."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/McWay_cove_1.jpg/330px-McWay_cove_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cove","wikidata":"Q31615"},{"title":"Seashell (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Seashell is an off-white color that resembles some of the very pale pinkish tones that are common in many seashells."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/White_ribbed_Anadara_valve_on_sand_in_Venezuela.jpg/330px-White_ribbed_Anadara_valve_on_sand_in_Venezuela.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seashell_(color)","wikidata":"Q7441815"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Shell_Island_1985.jpg/500px-Shell_Island_1985.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Shell_Island_1985.jpg/1280px-Shell_Island_1985.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Shell_Island_1985.jpg/500px-Shell_Island_1985.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AShell_Island_1985.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/8f/Selection_of_seashells.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/8f/Selection_of_seashells.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Hand-picked molluscan seashells (bivalves and gastropods) from the beach at Clacton on Sea in England","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASelection_of_seashells.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Seashells.JPG/500px-Seashells.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Seashells.JPG/1280px-Seashells.JPG?utm_sourc